From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Garcia-Madico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:48:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/37] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: remove a stream's channels by
 default

Without CHAN_CTRL(REMOVE) the ADSP only forgets a stream's channels when the
NGD runtime-suspends and the bus powers down, which almost never happens
inside a call. Moving a Bluetooth call away from the headset and back left
both directions silent, and on the Nothing Phone (1) a SLIMBUS_7_TX capture
started right after a failed one came back as exact zeros until the bus had
gone idle. A modprobe option was setting it; make it the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index cd7cf910e..eed889ffc 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -91,7 +91,14 @@
 /* Channel control operations in SLIM_USR_MC_CHAN_CTRL, as downstream */
 #define SLIM_CH_CTRL_REMOVE	2
 
-static bool remove_channels;
+/*
+ * On by default. Without it the ADSP only forgets a stream's channels when the
+ * NGD runtime-suspends and the bus powers down, which almost never happens
+ * inside a call: moving a Bluetooth call away from the headset and back left
+ * both directions silent, and a capture started right after a failed one came
+ * back as exact zeros.
+ */
+static bool remove_channels = true;
 module_param(remove_channels, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(remove_channels,
 		 "Tell the ADSP manager to remove a stream's channels when it is disabled");
